WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:09.770
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:20.300
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.490
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:06.970
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:14.240
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:20.980
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:28.410
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.990
With the death of Sibylla Mamina…

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.280
…and the ancient Simouns
now in the hands of Shoukoku…

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.000
…you could say they’ve
leveled the playing field.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.420
No, considering their
battle expertise…

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.750
…they now pose a
considerable threat.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.350
Just as we thought.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.010
It was reckless to send in
Chor Tempest after all…

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.810
But Chor Tempest did cause damage
to the aerial base, didn’t it?

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.430
The enemy will need
time to regroup…

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:10.000
…so I hardly think they’ll
be attacking anytime soon.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.770
That sibylla’s death
bought us some time.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:13.820
Am I wrong about that?

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.780
Remember that Tempus Spatium is
watching over everything you do.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:30.000
<b>Lament</b>

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.360
Dominüra…

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.380
…and Rimone…

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.030
I bet they’re dead too!

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:01.820
Floe…

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.510
They all…

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.620
They all died!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.760
And it’s going to keep happening!

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.290
All of us here!

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.290
We’re all going to die.
I just know it!

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:22.510
— You’re too much.
— What do you mean by that?

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.380
War is just a name
for killing each other.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:30.770
If you can’t accept that, then you
need to go to the Spring right away.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.980
But why… did it
have to be Mamina?

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.670
But why… did it
have to be Mamina?

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.730
I can’t even shed tears over this.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.180
The day Amuria died…

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.560
I think that maybe my own
heart died along with her.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.560
I’ve caused others pain…

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.560
Rejected their advances…

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.440
Yet despite it all, here I am,
unable to shed a tear…

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.530
Living on with a heart
that’s already dead.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.870
Yes.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.750
If only I’d died instead of Mamina.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.550
The Emerald…

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.310
Have you been here all this time?

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.900
Have you been crying?

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.190
If only…

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:09.860
…I’d been stronger.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.580
Mamina wouldn’t have died!

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.420
If only I’d…

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.500
No.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.490
I’m the one to blame,
because I was her pair.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:23.310
You had nothing to do with it.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.410
Don’t say that I had
nothing to do with it!

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.200
Aer…

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.700
Why are you crying?

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:51.200
What happened to the Aer who
wasn’t afraid of anything?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.540
Amuria!

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.830
I said I want to become stronger.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.500
You understand, right, Neviril?

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:04.580
We can do it.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.840
I’ve got to live.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.790
I… I’ve got to live.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:19.960
To live.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:28.930
Behind me lies the finest sibylla
in all of Simulacrum Kyuukoku…

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.040
…Sibylla Aurea Neviril.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.870
I’m getting her out
of here no matter what.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.870
And not one of you will lay
so much as a finger on her!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:39.720
You’re right.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:41.950
We’ve got to live on.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.080
Do you want something to drink?

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:30.830
Patch things up? That sounds like
we were actually friends before.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.190
Till the end, one of us
will always be above…

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:36.090
…and the other below.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.310
That’s not true.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:41.190
Anyway, just what were
you thinking that day?

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.240
That I wanted to be friends…

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:44.230
Don’t joke.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:50.240
It’s because I really want
to be friends with you all.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:55.570
Mamina!

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:58.480
So stop saying things like,
“We’re friends,” will you?

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.550
It’s just a matter of
how you feel about me.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:01.750
Okay.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.330
I’ll stop then.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:21.980
I have summoned
Onasia from the Spring.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.730
And the military council?

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.830
As you have ordered,
they know nothing.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:31.680
They only have eyes for warfare.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.320
It is truly deplorable.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.720
Hatred has tarnished the land.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:41.790
And yet they still cling to
this meaningless dispute…

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:45.420
…which can only lead to mutual
annihilation in battle. Such foolishness!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.380
There is no time to lose.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.770
We must find our way out of this
cursed land as soon as possible.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:56.040
We must follow the path
of Tempus Spatium…

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.890
…and open the door
to a new world!

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.600
A new world?

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.590
Yes, and to that end…

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:04.060
Anubituf…

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.220
There is much that I must
ask you to accomplish.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:08.310
First of all…

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.170
The phantom chor.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.860
Chor Dextra must be resurrected!

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:22.970
Granted, they’re somewhat inferior
to the Simouns in performance.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.000
But other than that, there
are no major differences.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.220
Sibylla Morinas.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.650
Is Sibylla Neviril’s Simoun…

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:39.760
No.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.260
Dismantling the ancient
Simoun’s your priority.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.120
All else will have
to wait, I suppose?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.170
Oh, not that I’m
blaming you or anything!

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:50.150
I’m sure you can’t rebel
against your superiors.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.110
Actually…

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.400
It was what I
wanted to do as well.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.610
Sibylla Morinas…

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.740
Would you please
go to the Spring?

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.020
I can’t do that right now.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.970
The Simouns are cursed!

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.900
I don’t care about the Simouns.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:19.690
Sibylla…

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.490
“As long as I can fly a
Simoun, nothing else matters!”

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.730
“Who cares about my comrades?”
At least, that’s what I used to think.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.680
But it seems I was
wrong about that.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:31.020
You’ve changed, Sibylla.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.480
So have you.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.090
Now that Mamina’s gone…

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:55.920
…do you think they’re going
to reshuffle our pairs again?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.420
Yes, I suppose so.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:02.550
But for all of us to pair up…
we’re short one person.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.680
What do you think, Para-sama?

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.260
Hey, Para-sama.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.480
Don’t ask me.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.190
Because…

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:19.270
…I don’t have any
answers for you.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.240
Para-sama…

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:29.790
Mamina is dead. How do
I tell her I’m sorry?

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:32.900
All I could think about
was my own problems…

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.720
…and I wasn’t performing as
a member of Chor Tempest should.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:39.950
It’s hopeless.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.670
Since when? And how?

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:44.960
How did I come to this?

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:46.790
How?

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.490
Para-sama.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:53.810
Alty?

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.560
It doesn’t have to be for real.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.690
What?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.700
Just be Para-sama,
no matter what.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:08.830
It doesn’t matter if they’re wrong,
just make bold decisions!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.290
I know you’re
suffering too, Paraietta!

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:12.720
But…

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:16.910
By simply being our
heroic Para-sama…

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.210
…you give us all
a little bit of hope.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:22.160
You say “us all,” but
you mean Kaim, right?

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:27.350
Why would you go so far for Kaim?

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.810
I just wanted to see
my sister smile again.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.690
The reason why I wanted
to become a man…

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:33.510
Why I wanted to become stronger…

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.230
It was all because I wanted
to make my sister happy.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:38.760
But I finally realized something.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.070
That something’s keeping
my sister from smiling…

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.440
…and it’s because
I’m in her way.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.870
And if that’s the case, there’s
only one thing I can do for her.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.840
For my sister’s sake…

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.510
…I’ll separate myself from her.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.560
Paraietta-sama!

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.070
Paraietta-sama!

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.320
It’s Sibylla Floe!

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.650
Floe?

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.030
What’s going on?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.210
Floe!

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.710
Floe! What are you
doing with that suitcase?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.050
I’m going!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.800
— What do you mean you’re going?
— I’m going to the Spring!

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:49.430
It’s no use trying to stop me!

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.140
I have no intention
of going to war…

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.560
…and I have no
intention of dying!

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:56.560
Hold on! We should all
talk about this first.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:02.460
Roatreamon.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.240
What’s that?

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.100
What, for heaven’s sake?

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.760
Is it a patrol Simile?

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.260
Where would it be
going at this hour?

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.290
Mamina…

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.230
Sibylla Mamina’s
remains have been…

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:45.570
…sent to her land where
she was born and raised.

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:53.490
But why? Why did you…

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.970
It was the high priestess’s wish.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:59.240
She felt that in order to
comfort Sibylla Mamina’s soul…

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:02.460
…it would be best to return
her to her beloved homeland.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:07.460
But you could’ve done that after her
funeral service here on the Arcus Prima!

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:10.130
You’re absolutely right.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:13.650
As a Simoun sibylla
who died with honor…

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:16.220
…it was our job to see that
she was given a proper burial.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.980
Died… with honor?

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:20.940
Come in.

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:26.610
Vura!

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:30.740
Sibylla Vura. In place
of Sibylla Mamina…

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.370
…she will be flying
a Simoun with you all.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.700
But wait!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:39.110
It is imperative that we rearrange
your pairs as soon as possible.

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:42.440
As well as achieve even
more powerful Ri Majons.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:44.210
Military Councilor!

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:47.710
We have just lost one
of our precious comrades!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.860
Ri Majons require our souls to be clear.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:54.300
We must be able to pray
with the purest of minds!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.260
We are not ready…

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.680
You speak as if you have
no cares in the world!

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.180
What?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:02.230
Do you wish Sibylla Mamina
to have died in vain?

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:16.950
You’re…

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.340
It’s just too cruel.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.060
How could they not let
us even say goodbye?

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:33.550
The military councilor’s
no different.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:37.470
All he can think about is war. He’s not
really thinking about Mamina at all!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.780
It’s because Mamina…

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:47.310
Because she wasn’t from
a Simoun sibylla family.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.810
It’s just like Mamina said.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:56.840
I’m just a pampered
rich girl after all!

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:58.590
And Mamina’s feelings.

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:00.660
I wanted to understand them.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:01.760
But…

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:03.370
But it turns out I
didn’t understand a thing!

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.120
Do you want to understand?

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:08.710
Yun.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.460
Mamina’s feelings…
They’re right here.

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:26.390
It resides here…

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:29.400
…Sibylla Mamina’s soul.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:36.400
And this soul… it has
accepted that her life is over.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:37.460
What?

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:41.410
In her eyes, it was
a meaningful death.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:42.910
Who…

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:45.950
You mustn’t touch Onasia-sama.

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:48.770
Bring it to me.

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:49.920
Yes, madam.

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:57.150
“Accepted that her life is over?”

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:59.050
I hate when people
say things like that!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.550
Floe…

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.620
That’s just to make
us feel better!

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:05.810
How can anyone really know
what the dead are feeling?

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:07.810
Roatreamon…

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:21.370
I was always envious of
those braids of yours.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:23.600
But these are…

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:27.500
You plait your hair because
your parents told you to.

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:32.040
But those things don’t
mean a thing to a child.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.210
To me, they were a
rich girl’s hairstyle.

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:37.510
That day…

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:42.890
…I really wanted to
be friends with Mamina.

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.390
That’s why I…

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.390
Just what do you
think you’re doing?

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.480
That’s why I…

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:55.570
She really wanted to
be friends with us all.

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:04.230
Mamina!

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:06.530
Mamina!

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.430
Mamina is a Simoun sibylla!

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:26.600
That’s right!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:33.100
And we Simoun sibylla didn’t
come here to go to war!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.070
Right!

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:38.820
Right!

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.110
Right!

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:42.100
Roatreamon!

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.370
Let’s go!

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.830
For all of you to go, you
need one more person, right?

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.380
Vura!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.050
All of my Rubor comrades
have gone to the Spring.

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.850
But I decided to
stay here anyway…

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:02.090
…for the same reason Mamina did!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:04.590
Because I wanted to
stay a Simoun sibylla!

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:10.810
Vura… thank you!

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:26.780
Sibylla!

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:28.950
Please!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.210
What on earth?

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.920
Who’s allowing them
to take such liberties?

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:49.930
How dare they,
in a time of emergency?

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.830
We’ll begin with one
that Mamina excelled at…

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.440
…the Wave Crest Ri Majon!

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.230
Roger!

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.740
Next, let’s do the
Dandelion Ri Majon!

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:24.220
Just as we thought…

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.260
Yes.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.180
Right! We’re all…

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:33.910
Aer…

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.530
Sibyllae!

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:54.540
Who inscribe our
prayers across the skies.

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:01.610
Sibyllae.

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:08.550
We pray for the future that
will go on forever and ever…

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:13.260
And for the past that we’ve
already woven, we offer our prayers!

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:20.960
Sibyllae…

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:23.930
Yes…

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:26.260
That’s who we are!

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:47.970
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:52.200
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:59.270
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:06.870
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:24.930
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:28.910
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:32.950
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:38.820
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.820 --> 00:23:44.360
<i>Soar away into the
sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.800
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:53.460
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:59.690
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:09.690
Bestowed upon us by Tempus Spatium…

00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:11.800
…the other “if.”

00:24:13.590 --> 00:24:15.550
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:17.780
The Door to a New World.

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>The Door to a New World</b>
